<style>
  .coffee-content { font-family: "Helvetica Neue", "Helvetica Now Text", Arial, sans-serif; --s: 1; }
  .screen--lg .coffee-content { --s: 1.3; }
  .coffee-layout { display: flex; flex-wrap: nowrap; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 100%; }
  .coffee-layout.stack { flex-direction: column; }
  .coffee-layout.stack .coffee-title { text-align: center; } /* row layouts stay left-aligned, matching the list below them */
  .coffee-meta { flex: 0 1 auto; min-width: 90px; }

  .coffee-title {
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    border-bottom: 4px solid #111;
    display: inline-block;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #111;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .view--full .coffee-title { border-bottom: calc(6px * var(--s, 1)) solid #111; } /* thicker underline — full has the room for it */
  .coffee-subtitle { font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", monospace; color: #555; margin: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }

  .cup {
    border: 3px solid #111;
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column-reverse; /* first ingredient in the array = bottom, matching pour order */
    flex-shrink: 0;
    position: relative;
    max-height: 100%; /* safety cap: a maxed-out glass (360ml) in a short layout would otherwise overflow */
  }
  .vessel-demitasse { border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px; }
  .vessel-mug { border-radius: 0 0 14px 14px; }
  /* glass + martini aren't rectangles — an SVG draws the outline (its stroke follows the path
     exactly), and a same-shaped clip-path div underneath carries the liquid layers */
  .vessel-glass, .vessel-martini { border: none; overflow: visible; }
  .vessel-fill { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column-reverse; overflow: hidden; }
  .vessel-outline { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none; }
  /* TRMNL's OG panels are 1-bit/2-bit e-ink — two fills that look distinct on a normal screen can
     dither to the same bucket on-device (this is why the palette below only uses 4 stops). A hard
     seam between stacked layers means adjacent bands still read as separate even if a color pair
     ever collapses, instead of silently merging into one block. */
  .layer { width: 100%; }
  .layer + .layer { border-top: 2px solid #111; }
  .view--full .layer + .layer { border-top: calc(4px * var(--s, 1)) solid #111; }

  .ice-cubes { position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; }
  .cube { position: absolute; width: 22%; aspect-ratio: 1; background: #f0f0f0; border: 1.5px solid #111; border-radius: 2px; }

  .ingredients { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; line-height: 1.6; color: #555; }
  .ingredients li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; }
  .dot { width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #111; flex-shrink: 0; }
</style>

{% comment %}
  Title font size is solved from the drink name's length, not picked from a fixed base — a short
  name (Mocha) gets a bigger font than a long one (Espresso Con Panna) so it actually fills the
  text column instead of leaving it half-empty. target_w is that column's real rendered width
  (measured per variant — TRMNL's framework reserves more margin than the nominal screen width
  suggests, so this is calibrated against real output, not the CSS spec), c is the measured average
  char-width-to-font-size ratio for this bold uppercase face. Params: name, target_w, c, min_px, max_px
{% endcomment %}
{% template title_fit %}
{% assign len = name.size %}
{% if len < 1 %}{% assign len = 1 %}{% endif %}
{% assign px = target_w | times: 1.0 | divided_by: len | divided_by: c | round %}
{% if px > max_px %}{% assign px = max_px %}{% endif %}
{% if px < min_px %}{% assign px = min_px %}{% endif %}
{{ px }}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} Cup/gap/ingredient-text size multiplier — vertical room gets eaten two ways: more
  ingredients means more lines, and a single long label (e.g. "Steamed Milk, Ice, Whipped Cream &
  Caramel Syrup") wraps to 2 lines on its own even with just one item. Both shrink cup+gap+text
  together so a tall glass/martini plus wrapped label text doesn't push past the card's bottom
  edge (the title is sized separately, by width, in title_fit above). Params: ingredients (array)
{% endcomment %}
{% template count_scale %}
{% assign n = ingredients.size %}
{% assign max_len = 0 %}
{% for ing in ingredients %}{% if ing.label.size > max_len %}{% assign max_len = ing.label.size %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% assign factor = 1.0 %}
{% if n > 4 %}{% assign factor = 0.8 %}
{% elsif n > 3 %}{% assign factor = 0.88 %}
{% elsif n > 2 %}{% assign factor = 0.95 %}
{% endif %}
{% if max_len > 30 %}{% assign factor = factor | times: 0.72 %}
{% elsif max_len > 20 %}{% assign factor = factor | times: 0.85 %}
{% endif %}
{{ factor }}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} Grayscale palette — the e-ink panel has no color mode, so this is the real palette,
  not a simulation. OG panels are 1-bit/2-bit: only ~4 distinguishable levels actually exist on
  the device, so this uses exactly 4 stops (black/dark/light/white) snapped to where a 2-bit panel
  quantizes (0/85/170/255) instead of continuous in-between values a real panel would just round
  away — two "different" grays that both round to the same bucket is how Foamed Milk and Steamed
  Milk merged into one block on-device (the divider in the CSS above is the other half of that
  fix). Darkest = most concentrated (espresso), lightest = airiest (whipped cream). "vanilla ice
  cream" must stay ahead of the bare "ice" check, or every Affogato's scoop would render as an ice
  cube instead of its own tone. {% endcomment %}
{% template ingredient_color %}{% assign l = label | downcase %}{% if l contains 'espresso' %}#000000{% elsif l contains 'brewed coffee' or l contains 'french pressed' or l contains 'iced coffee' or l contains 'coffee liqueur' or l contains 'chocolate' or l contains 'caramel' or l contains 'whiskey' or l contains 'brandy' %}#555555{% elsif l contains 'half & half' or l contains 'steamed milk' or l contains 'scalded milk' or l contains 'condensed milk' or l contains 'sugar' or l contains 'vodka' %}#aaaaaa{% elsif l contains 'foam' or l contains 'lemon' or l contains 'vanilla ice cream' or l contains 'ice' or l contains 'hot water' or l contains 'whipped cream' %}#ffffff{% else %}#aaaaaa{% endif %}{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  Renders the cup: classifies a vessel shape from the ingredients, sizes it from total_ml, then
  draws the proportional layer bars (a bare "Ice" ingredient is skipped — it's cubes floating in
  whatever's underneath, not a poured layer — drawn separately below instead).
  Params: ingredients (array), total_ml (number), scale (float, per-layout size multiplier)
{% endcomment %}
{% template cup %}
{% assign has_ice = false %}
{% assign has_spirit = false %}
{% assign has_milk = false %}
{% for ing in ingredients %}
  {% assign l = ing.label | downcase %}
  {% if l contains 'vodka' or l contains 'liqueur' %}{% assign has_spirit = true %}{% endif %}
  {% comment %} a dot of foam (Macchiato, 10ml) shouldn't count as "has milk" — it's still a
    demitasse-sized shot, not a milk drink. Liquid has no parens and evaluates and/or strictly
    left-to-right, so the ml check has to be a separate step or it only binds to the first clause. {% endcomment %}
  {% assign is_milk_label = false %}
  {% if l contains 'steamed milk' or l contains 'foamed milk' or l contains 'half & half' or l contains 'scalded milk' %}{% assign is_milk_label = true %}{% endif %}
  {% if is_milk_label and ing.ml > 15 %}{% assign has_milk = true %}{% endif %}
  {% unless l == 'vanilla ice cream' %}{% if l contains 'ice' %}{% assign has_ice = true %}{% endif %}{% endunless %}
{% endfor %}

{% comment %} straight shot -> demitasse, ice -> tapered glass, vodka/liqueur -> coupe on a stem
  (Irish coffee has whiskey but no vodka/liqueur, so it stays a mug), everything else -> mug {% endcomment %}
{% assign vessel = 'mug' %}
{% if has_ice %}
  {% assign vessel = 'glass' %}
{% elsif has_spirit %}
  {% assign vessel = 'martini' %}
{% elsif total_ml <= 75 and has_milk == false %}
  {% assign vessel = 'demitasse' %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %} base size range per vessel (px @ scale 1), interpolated by where total_ml falls in
  the 15-360ml spread across the whole recipe list, e.g. a Ristretto's demitasse is smaller than
  a Macchiato's, a Latte's mug bigger than a Cortado's {% endcomment %}
{% case vessel %}
  {% when 'demitasse' %}{% assign minw = 30 %}{% assign maxw = 42 %}{% assign minh = 36 %}{% assign maxh = 54 %}
  {% when 'glass' %}{% assign minw = 40 %}{% assign maxw = 58 %}{% assign minh = 84 %}{% assign maxh = 144 %}
  {% when 'martini' %}{% assign minw = 58 %}{% assign maxw = 82 %}{% assign minh = 56 %}{% assign maxh = 92 %}
{% else %}{% assign minw = 42 %}{% assign maxw = 62 %}{% assign minh = 64 %}{% assign maxh = 130 %}
{% endcase %}
{% assign t = total_ml | minus: 15 | times: 1.0 | divided_by: 345 %}
{% if t < 0 %}{% assign t = 0 %}{% endif %}
{% if t > 1 %}{% assign t = 1 %}{% endif %}
{% assign wr = maxw | minus: minw %}
{% assign hr = maxh | minus: minh %}
{% assign width = t | times: wr | plus: minw | times: scale | round %}
{% assign height = t | times: hr | plus: minh | times: scale | round %}

{% assign glass_clip = 'polygon(2% 2%, 98% 2%, 84% 98%, 16% 98%)' %}
{% assign martini_clip = 'polygon(3% 4%, 97% 4%, 53% 78%, 47% 78%)' %}
{% if vessel == 'glass' or vessel == 'martini' %}
  {% assign clip = glass_clip %}
  {% if vessel == 'martini' %}{% assign clip = martini_clip %}{% endif %}
  <div class="cup vessel-{{ vessel }}" style="width:calc({{ width }}px * var(--s, 1));height:calc({{ height }}px * var(--s, 1))">
    <div class="vessel-fill" style="clip-path:{{ clip }}">
      {% for ing in ingredients %}
        {% assign l = ing.label | downcase %}
        {% unless l == 'ice' %}
          {% capture color %}{% render "ingredient_color", label: ing.label %}{% endcapture %}
          <div class="layer" style="flex:{{ ing.ml }} 0 0; background:{{ color | strip }}"></div>
        {% endunless %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <svg class="vessel-outline" viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none">
      {% if vessel == 'glass' %}
        <path d="M2 2 L98 2 L84 98 L16 98 Z" style="fill:none;stroke:#111;stroke-width:3"></path>
      {% else %}
        <path d="M3 4 L97 4 L53 78 L47 78 Z" style="fill:none;stroke:#111;stroke-width:3"></path>
        <line x1="50" y1="78" x2="50" y2="93" style="stroke:#111;stroke-width:3"></line>
        <line x1="30" y1="96" x2="70" y2="96" style="stroke:#111;stroke-width:3"></line>
      {% endif %}
    </svg>
    {% if has_ice %}
      <div class="ice-cubes" style="clip-path:{{ clip }}">
        <span class="cube" style="left:8%;top:6%;transform:rotate(-10deg)"></span>
        <span class="cube" style="left:44%;top:14%;transform:rotate(14deg)"></span>
        <span class="cube" style="left:22%;top:28%;transform:rotate(-18deg)"></span>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
{% else %}
  <div class="cup vessel-{{ vessel }}" style="width:calc({{ width }}px * var(--s, 1));height:calc({{ height }}px * var(--s, 1))">
    {% for ing in ingredients %}
      {% assign l = ing.label | downcase %}
      {% unless l == 'ice' %}
        {% capture color %}{% render "ingredient_color", label: ing.label %}{% endcapture %}
        <div class="layer" style="flex:{{ ing.ml }} 0 0; background:{{ color | strip }}"></div>
      {% endunless %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% if has_ice %}
      <div class="ice-cubes">
        <span class="cube" style="left:8%;top:6%;transform:rotate(-10deg)"></span>
        <span class="cube" style="left:44%;top:14%;transform:rotate(14deg)"></span>
        <span class="cube" style="left:22%;top:28%;transform:rotate(-18deg)"></span>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  Ingredient list, top layer first / base last — mirrors looking at the cup top-to-bottom
  (the cup itself stacks bottom-up in DOM order via column-reverse, so this is the reverse of
  that array order). Params: ingredients (array), text_size (px, OG baseline — scales via --s)
{% endcomment %}
{% template ingredient_list %}
<ul class="ingredients" style="font-size:calc({{ text_size }}px * var(--s, 1))">
  {% for ing in ingredients reversed %}
    {% capture color %}{% render "ingredient_color", label: ing.label %}{% endcapture %}
    <li><span class="dot" style="background:{{ color | strip }}"></span>{{ ing.label }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endtemplate %}
